<title>JAPAN: TOCOM to raise palladium futures margin fees.</title>
<headline>TOCOM to raise palladium futures margin fees.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tokyo Commodity Exchange said on Friday that it will raise margin requirements for all of its palladium futures contracts by 20,000 yen per trading lot, effective from next Tuesday.</p>
<p>The move will bring the total March requirement to 94,250 yen, while margins for other months will rise to 69,500 yen, the exchange said in a statement.</p>
<p>The increases were intended to cool overheated trade, it said.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodity Desk +81-3-3432-7431</p>
